[x] grammar rejects malformed UUIDs as syntax errors instead of letting the linter flag them $ E006_invalid_uuid inputs like #123 or #abc-def parse to syntax-error + missing-id, so the E006 invalid-uuid lint rule never fires — tests/linting_conformance.rs test_linting_error_detection has been red on main since 6861516 ("linting more hardcore") tightened the id grammar. this is a Decision 6 violation: the tree-sitter grammar should accept a malformed #id permissively and let the E006 linter catch the bad format, not error the whole line. worse, a syntax-error can drop the action from loads entirely — the same silent-dropout class the [[trust]] doctor fsck targets. DONE 2026-07-03: id rule now accepts a malformed_id fallback token (patterns.js + grammar.js) so any #<text> forms an id node; the parser was already correct (Uuid::parse_str failure captures raw_id). the lint side became two mutually-exclusive checks off raw_id: E006 (error) for a genuinely invalid id, and the NEW W013 (warning) for an INCOMPLETE uuid — a well-formed prefix with a dash in a template slot (12345678-1234, 01950000-0000-7000-8000), the live-buffer case that lint-warns not errors (Decision 6). is_incomplete_uuid draws the boundary; the E006 fixture shrank to genuine mistakes and a W013 fixture was added. test_linting_error_detection is green $ !2 +bug,library %2026-07-03T00:00#019f2abc-af8d-76c4-a1a5-65e9c7ffcc12
[x] read actions filters (--open-only, --context) do not exclude non-matching actions $ tests/read_actions.rs has 4 red tests (open_only_excludes_completed_and_cancelled, context_filter_selects_matching_tag, context_filter_with_tag_hierarchy_matches_descendants, open_only_and_context_filter_combine): the JSON output still contains actions that should be filtered out (a completed "Done task" survives --open-only; an "Other task" +personal survives --context work). PRE-EXISTING and unrelated to the E006 grammar work — proven red on the clean committed base by stashing the core+grammar changes and re-running the suite. DONE 2026-07-03: the --format json/jsonld branch of read_actions_cmd serialized the whole workspace model unfiltered (ignored action_filter, charter, plan) — only the table and TTY-tree paths applied the filter. extracted filtered_primary_model (charter narrowing + apply_filter), now shared by the JSON-LD and TTY branches so every output mode honors the same filters. all 6 read_actions tests green $ !2 +bug,cli %2026-07-03T00:00#019f2b73-3786-7edd-b503-28aa939db573
[ ] grammar-example and linting-example snapshots were stale after caldav + multi-tag landed $ found while running the full CLI suite 2026-07-03: tests/snapshots_from_examples snapshots predated two committed core changes — the caldav sync fields (scheduled_at_sync/due_date_sync on Action, commit 2c074bf) and the multi-tag context fix (+work,,,+errands now preserves all comma entries, not just the last). regenerated all snapshots to match; the diff was only the two None sync fields per action plus the recovered context entries. no behavior change, pure snapshot maintenance. logging in case there is a CI gap that let these rot unnoticed $ +testing,cli %2026-07-03T00:00#019f2b93-39ee-71f7-931e-bb2dac390239
